{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791755468,"nonce":"ocINooCs7Y2B0iukGgldzGiBVm8=","title":"Returning an existing Bytes buffer allocates in both JIT tiers","message":"ChimpMonk's new input recording hot path exposed allocation in haxe.io.Bytes.getData(). A reduced three-arm fixture repeatedly writes through the returned pointer, writes through a pointer cached before the loop, and blits through that cached pointer. All arms assert their final bytes, with 8,192 calls and seven allocation windows after warmup; ASH_GC_TLAB=0.\n\nReproducer: /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/chimpmonk/repro/ash_bytes_get_data_alloc/Repro.hx and its README. Initial probe /tmp/chimpmonk-input/BytesAllocProbe.hx and /tmp/chimpmonk-input/bytes-alloc.hl reports getData 262,064 allocated bytes, cached/direct byte copies zero, in default hybrid --preset game, pinned Cranelift and pinned LLVM. The getter is returning the same existing hl.Bytes allocation; the cost is not a request for fresh buffer storage. Root cause has not yet been isolated to a specific ABI or lowering path.\n\nLocal Ash release: 0.1.5; SHA256 d2616edb918775c55281049991bfef11c13d96deebdebff4fced8ce626b229bf. No Ash sources or binary changed during this investigation. Recompile Repro.hx with haxe -cp /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/chimpmonk/repro/ash_bytes_get_data_alloc -main Repro -hl /tmp/bytes-get-data.hl, then env ASH_GC_TLAB=0 /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/ash/target/release/ash --preset game /tmp/bytes-get-data.hl; pin each tier as in the README.\n\nDesired outcome: compatible byte-pointer getters avoid boxing/allocation in both tiers, preserving returned pointer identity and aliasing, native byte reads/writes and exception behaviour. Add an exact allocation regression and validate both JIT tiers/default hybrid, plus hot reload and dynamic/unsupported signature fallback if the fix touches dispatch.\n\nChimpMonk caches the recording's byte pointer during construction. Sampling, edge evaluation, binary recording and playback now allocate zero after warmup; this local caching keeps its input work progressing while the runtime opportunity remains visible here. Input issue: 5486670992f14413ebfb9d405e2571d6aafab8fe7182a5a8701aea99a089e8c1.","files":null}]}